The projection points opposite to $\underset{\sim}{b}$ because the angle is obtuse. Its magnitude is $12|\cos120^{\circ}|=6$.
Using the right triangle formed by the two components:
$\begin{aligned}\left|\underset{\sim}{a}-\text{proj}_{\underset{\sim}{b}}\underset{\sim}{a}\right|^2&=12^2-6^2\\&=108\\\left|\underset{\sim}{a}-\text{proj}_{\underset{\sim}{b}}\underset{\sim}{a}\right|&=6\sqrt{3}\end{aligned}$
Equivalently, use the booklet's perpendicular-component magnitude formula:
$\begin{aligned}\left|\underset{\sim}{a}-\text{proj}_{\underset{\sim}{b}}\underset{\sim}{a}\right|&=|\underset{\sim}{a}|\sin\theta\\&=12\sin120^{\circ}\\&=12\times\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\\&=6\sqrt{3}\end{aligned}$
